{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Self-drilling screws complement my recent rivets, rivet nuts, and bolts by giving me another useful way to fasten sheet metal.",
    "Threaded magnets extend my interest in mounting supplies to removable attachments, while pegboards would help keep my growing tool and fastener collection accessible.",
    "Heat-shrink tubing feels useful for protecting connections during repairs without requiring a particular wire-splicing job."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another grommet installation tool and a similar borescope duplicate equipment I already have, with no clear new capability I currently need.",
    "The sound meter, electrical test leads, and solder-seal connectors serve specific tasks I do not have underway; being repair-related does not make them useful to me now.",
    "Printer filament assumes a printing need that my recent purchases do not establish, and I have no particular use for blue filament."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying workshop supplies seems to have been taken as interest in almost any technical tool, even when it serves a different task.",
    "Buying a particular tool seems to invite more versions of that tool, although my purchase may have already filled that need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, threaded inserts, bolts, and cutting supplies make complementary fabrication and fastening supplies especially relevant right now.",
    "My newest grommet press already includes several dies and grommets, so compatible replenishments would make more sense than another installation tool.",
    "I distinguish broadly useful repair supplies from equipment that needs a specific project or a clear reason to replace something I own."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my workshop interests but sometimes confuse useful additions with duplicate equipment or supplies for projects I have not shown a need for."
}"}
